# D1 rebuttal replay — ROUND 1 (reviews): the paper plus the review round
#
# Round 1 is round 0 (examples/rebuttal-replay/round0) plus three reviewer comments lowered as
# typed attacks. The artifact and policy are unchanged (single-artifact: the reviews are ABOUT the
# paper, not a new artifact). Each reviewer comment becomes a typed attack against an existing
# argument; reviewer-cited external evidence enters as `attested` leaves with OpenReview refs.
#
# Reviewer comments and their lowering (one per attack kind; see docs/demos/d1-rebuttal-replay.md):
#   * Reviewer 1 (UNDERMINE): "Your OpenLLM protocol was not held fixed — hyperparameters were tuned
#     on the eval tasks, so the fixed-protocol claim does not hold." Lowered as an undermine of
#     a_bench's protocol_fixed leaf (pb2) via the declared contrary not_fixed_protocol/fixed_protocol.
#   * Reviewer 2 (REBUT): "A concurrent replication finds APT does NOT match the dense baseline on
#     OpenLLM." Lowered as a null_benchmark argument concluding not_performs(...) — a declared
#     contrary of a_bench's conclusion — so it rebuts a_bench (mutual, by attack completeness).
#   * Reviewer 3 (UNDERCUT): "Your low-memory-footprint number is a measurement artifact of the
#     gradient-checkpointing you enabled only for APT." Lowered as an undercut of a_meas at its rule,
#     via corpus-v1's declared exception measurement : measurement_artifact.
#
# The reviewers ALSO note the kurtosis ablation is single-run ("add error bars"): that is not a
# typed attack — it is the already-unmet mandatory variance CQ that keeps c_kurt `gap`. The
# framework flagged it at submission; the reviewer merely agrees. Round 2 discharges it.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact adaptive-pruning at sha256:de3685165a53
policy rebuttal-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# ===============================================================================================
# THE PAPER (unchanged from round 0)
# ===============================================================================================

# --- c_bench: benchmark performance vs the dense baseline --------------------------------------

claim c_bench
  nl      = "APT at 30% sparsity performs competitively with the dense LLaMA2-7B baseline on the OpenLLM four-task average"
  formal  = performs(apt, dense_baseline, openllm_avg)
  binding = { author = apt-authors, audit-status = reviewed }

leaf pb1 : reports(e02, benchmark_result(apt, dense_baseline, openllm_avg, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02, Table-4]

leaf pb2 : fixed_protocol(apt, dense_baseline, e02)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E02-step-3]

leaf pb3 : valid_benchmark(dense_baseline, openllm_avg)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-Metrics]

arg a_bench : supports(c_bench) by benchmark_evaluation(apt, dense_baseline, openllm_avg, e02)
  discharge protocol_fixed    with pb2
  discharge benchmark_valid   with pb3
  open      environment_match as environment_match

# --- c_measure: low training-memory footprint -------------------------------------------------

claim c_measure
  nl      = "APT trains with a low peak-memory footprint (41.6 percent of the Prune+Distill baseline)"
  formal  = holds(low_memory_footprint, apt)
  binding = { author = apt-authors, audit-status = reviewed }

leaf pm1 : observes(e04, low_memory_footprint, apt)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E04, Table-10]

leaf pm2 : valid_instrument(low_memory_footprint, e04)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E04-step-2]

leaf pm3 : covers_scope(e04, apt)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E04-Setup]

arg a_meas : supports(c_measure) by measurement(low_memory_footprint, apt, e04)
  discharge instrument_validity with pm2
  discharge coverage            with pm3
  open      confound_control     as confound_control

# --- c_kurt: the kurtosis-salience ablation (still gap; reviewers ask for error bars) ----------

claim c_kurt
  nl      = "Removing the kurtosis (outlier-aware) salience term drops the LLaMA2-7B OpenLLM average from 50.0 to 38.1 at 30 percent sparsity, so the kurtosis term is critical for large-LM pruning"
  formal  = contributes(kurtosis_salience, apt_llama2_7b, openllm_avg)
  binding = { author = apt-authors, audit-status = reviewed }

leaf pk1 : reports(e03, ablation_effect(kurtosis_salience, apt_llama2_7b, openllm_avg, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03, Table-5, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N09-N10]

leaf pk2 : isolated(kurtosis_salience, e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-step-6]

leaf pk3 : matched_protocol(e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-step-7]

# ===============================================================================================
# THE REVIEW ROUND (new in round 1)
# ===============================================================================================

# --- Reviewer 1 (UNDERMINE): the OpenLLM protocol was not held fixed --------------------------
# Reviewer-cited evidence: the reviewer read the released config and found eval-task tuning. The
# leaf concludes not_fixed_protocol, the declared contrary of a_bench's protocol_fixed leaf pb2.
leaf ru_np : not_fixed_protocol(apt, dense_baseline, e02)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [openreview#R1-official-review-weakness-2]

arg d_um : challenges(pb2) by leaf(ru_np)
undermine d_um a_bench.protocol_fixed.leaf

# --- Reviewer 2 (REBUT): a concurrent replication finds APT does NOT match dense ---------------
# The reviewer cites an external replication (a negative benchmark result) with its own fixed
# protocol and matched environment — a complete null_benchmark argument concluding
# not_performs(apt, dense_baseline, openllm_avg), the declared contrary of a_bench's conclusion.
leaf ru_nb1 : reports(e_rep, benchmark_result(apt, dense_baseline, openllm_avg, negative))
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [openreview#R2-official-review-weakness-1]

leaf ru_nb2 : fixed_protocol(apt, dense_baseline, e_rep)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [openreview#R2-official-review-appendix]

leaf ru_nb3 : matched_environment(e_rep)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [openreview#R2-official-review-appendix]

arg d_rebut : supports(c_bench_neg) by null_benchmark(apt, dense_baseline, openllm_avg, e_rep)
  discharge protocol_fixed    with ru_nb2
  discharge environment_match with ru_nb3

# performs / not_performs are contrary in BOTH directions (rebuttal-v1), so attack completeness
# (spec §8) requires both rebut edges. a_bench is already driven out by the undermine, so the
# reverse edge does not change a_bench's label — but it must be declared to pass the checker.
rebut d_rebut a_bench
rebut a_bench d_rebut

# --- Reviewer 3 (UNDERCUT): the memory number is a measurement artifact ------------------------
# Licensed by the declared exception measurement : measurement_artifact(P, S). The challenge
# contests a_meas's instrument_validity; the undercut targets the rule application.
leaf ru_ma : measurement_artifact(low_memory_footprint, apt)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = user
  refs       = [openreview#R3-official-review-weakness-1]

arg d_meas : challenges(instrument_validity(a_meas)) by leaf(ru_ma)
undercut d_meas a_meas.rule

status c_bench
status c_measure
status c_kurt

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle) — verified by test/WorkedExamplesSpec.hs
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF (declaration order): a_bench (0), a_meas (1), d_um (2), d_rebut (3), d_meas (4).
#   a_bench (0) -> out   (LOut; undermined by d_um (in) and rebutted by d_rebut; either drives it out)
#   a_meas  (1) -> out   (LOut; undercut by the unattacked d_meas)
#   d_um    (2) -> in    (LIn; leaf-rooted, unattacked)
#   d_rebut (3) -> in    (LIn; its only attacker a_bench is out)
#   d_meas  (4) -> in    (LIn; leaf-rooted, unattacked)
# Claim statuses:
#   c_bench   -> defeated  (support a_bench is out)
#   c_measure -> defeated  (support a_meas is out)
#   c_kurt    -> gap       (still empty complete support; the "add error bars" comment is the
#                           unmet mandatory variance CQ, not a typed attack)
#
# Trajectory: c_bench justified -> defeated, c_measure justified -> defeated, c_kurt gap -> gap.
# Round 2 (rebuttal) reinstates c_bench, concedes c_measure, and discharges c_kurt.
